out-alleged-russian-bot-activity/a-79651769?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Did attacks on Russian data centers reduce bot activity around Germany's AfD? A viral graph claims they did. But it contains significant inconsistencies and provides no evidence to support the claim.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Political infighting deepens as economic woes mount during war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6472e7ef85ea169620b57cff372b32eec1e2e13cdeff879f1b2eef546011b6b</id><updated>2026-10-15T13:32:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T05:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-political-infighting-deepens-as-economic-woes-mount-during-war/a-79654461--e42dac42e7a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-political-infighting-deepens-as-economic-woes-mount-during-war/a-79654461?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hardliners are stepping up pressure on Iran's government and calling for Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi's removal. The oil minister resigned, but that's doing little to ease the pressure on President Masoud Pezeshkian.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
